From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:45:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(transport): per-run model request pacer from a shared
 sliding-window ledger

RHOAI3 Stage 080 (architect review R2): the declared request allowance of a
run must be enforced, not only checked. When RHOAI3_REQUEST_BUDGET=<n>/<s>
and RHOAI3_REQUEST_LEDGER=<path> are set, every model HTTP request any
Hermes process of the run sends takes one slot from an append-only,
flock-protected ledger shared by all processes and surviving restarts.
Unset => disabled, behaviour unchanged.

- agent/request_pacer.py: ledger, sliding window, wait for the oldest slot
  up to RHOAI3_REQUEST_BUDGET_MAX_WAIT (default 900 s), else raise
  RequestBudgetExhausted with a named STOP MODEL_REQUEST_BUDGET message
  (worded to avoid the dispatcher's quota/auth respawn-blocker pattern).
- Enforcement: an httpx request event hook attached at the OpenAI client
  construction choke points (agent_runtime_helpers primary client;
  auxiliary_client sync, async and Vertex clients), so each HTTP attempt,
  including every Hermes and SDK retry, takes exactly one slot (POST only).
- Main loop: wait_for_slot() before each API attempt so a long wait happens
  outside the stream stale detector and touches worker activity; a budget
  exhaustion is never retried and ends the turn with model_stop=
  request_budget, recorded by the shared kanban worker-stop recorder as a
  failed run.
